## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to translate regulatory requirements into automated, auditable technical controls using Azure AI and governance services, with strict multi-tenant isolation requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Regulatory-to-controls mapping (GDPR/CCPA/NIST)
- Knowledge base grounding with Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- Automated evidence collection and auditable logging
- Azure Policy integration for continuous enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Map obligations to controls and enforce per-tenant policy
async function ensureCompliance(clientId) {
  const obligations = await kb.fetchObligations(clientId);
  const controls = await mapToControls(obligations);

  const evidence = await collectEvidence(clientId, controls);
  const violations = await evaluateAgainstPolicy(controls, evidence);

  await logDecision({ clientId, obligations, controls, evidence, violations });
  return generateRemediationPlan(violations);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to architect a secure, scalable incident-response automation platform across tenants using Azure AI services. Covers real-time event ingestion, strict data isolation, guardrails for safe prompt generation, canary testing, and comprehensive audit logging.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time Event Hubs ingestion with tenant-scoped event routing
- Tenant-isolated Cognitive Search indexes for grounded KB retrieval
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before processing and storage
- Canary playbook execution behind API Management with traffic splitting policies
- Data Lake for raw audit logs, Cosmos DB for structured remediation results
- Azure AD RBAC for multi-tenant access control

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize per-tenant Cognitive Search client with Managed Identity
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SearchIndexClient } = require('@azure/search-documents');

async function getTenantSearchClient(tenantId) {
  const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
  const indexName = `kb-${tenantId}`;
  return new SearchIndexClient(
    `https://${process.env.SEARCH_SERVICE}.search.windows.net/`,
    indexName,
    credential
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multilingual, policy-respecting flows with Azure AI services and end-to-end data handling. Emphasizes privacy, per-tenant configuration, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI, API Management, Cognitive Search, Blob
- Azure Translator, Text Analytics for redaction
- Cosmos DB for tenant config, Data Lake for audit logs
- End-to-end data flow and test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// PII redaction and translation flow (pseudo)
async function prepareQuery(input, targetLang){
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const translated = await translateText(redacted, targetLang);
  const prompt = `Q: ${translated}\nA:`
  return prompt;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test translation accuracy across languages?
- How would you handle translation errors impacting latency?
